    content: `# 10-20-30 SLIDE DESIGN & VISUAL DELIVERY CHECKLIST
Presentation & Communication Academy | E-Learning Systems

## THE GOLDEN RULES OF COGNITIVE LOAD
When slides are crowded with text, your audience reads the slide and tunes out your voice. Slides are visual anchors, not teleprompter scripts!

## 1. THE 10/20/30 PRINCIPLE
- **10 Slides Maximum:** Forces you to cut trivial fluff and focus only on essential strategic milestones.
- **20 Minutes Maximum:** Keeps the monologue phase sharp and leaves ample time for interactive debate.
- **30-Point Minimum Font Size:** Ensures instant legibility from the back of any auditorium or on a mobile laptop screen.

## 2. SLIDE DESIGN CHECKLIST
[ ] One Core Idea Per Slide: Does this slide communicate exactly one takeaway?
[ ] Action Title: Does the slide header state a conclusion rather than a category?
    - Poor: "Q3 Sales Trends"
    - Effective: "Q3 Enterprise Sales Grew 24% Following New Onboarding"
[ ] 80/20 Visual Balance: Is at least 40% of the slide clean whitespace?
[ ] High-Contrast Palette: Dark text on clean light background or crisp white on deep navy.
[ ] Zero Generic Stock Photography: Use real charts, clear architecture diagrams, or relevant imagery.

## 3. DELIVERY CHECKLIST (TOUCH - TURN - TALK)
[ ] Touch: Step forward and gesture toward the focal point on the visual.
[ ] Turn: Pivot eyes and chest fully back toward the audience.
[ ] Talk: Deliver your spoken point while maintaining direct eye contact with the room.`
